# The Windows checkout is CRLF (core.autocrlf), but `docker build` copies from
# the working tree, and a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang makes the container exit with
# "no such file or directory". Pin shell scripts to LF so an image built on a
# developer machine is the same one CI builds.
#
# This does not repair a checkout that is already CRLF: eol=lf applies on
# checkout and add, so an existing working tree keeps building broken images
# until it is renormalised. Diagnose with `git ls-files --eol '*.sh'` (i/lf
# w/crlf is the stale state) and fix it with:
#     git add --renormalize '*.sh' && git checkout -- '*.sh'
# The renormalize stages current content first, so uncommitted edits survive.
*.sh text eol=lf
